  "title": "SpaceX Moon Crash Sparks New Moon Crater Image",
  "summary": "A NASA spacecraft captured images of a 60-foot-wide crater on the moon caused by a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket crash, marking the first time such a large impact event has been observed in over a decade. The event highlights the challenges faced by the rocket industry and the importance of space exploration.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "NASA's Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter captured images of a 60-foot-wide crater on the moon caused by a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket crash.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The crater appears to be 10 feet (3 meters) deep and shows signs of recent impact from solar wind and micrometeorite strikes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The event was first documented in over a decade after a similar large impact on the moon occurred in 2010.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
